  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height:normal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;100, 101, 102, Design and Access Statement (Moran Architecture, Feb 2026), Noise and Vibration Impact Assessment (Ref:26119 / 230C Northolt Road, date 12&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;/sup&gt; May 2026), Reasonable Exception Statement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The launderette hereby permitted shall operate only between the hours of 08:00 and 18:00 Monday to Sunday (including bank holidays), unless otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;Prior to the first commencement of the use hereby permitted, the acoustic insulation measures detailed in the submitted Noise and Vibration Impact Assessment shall be fully implemented and thereafter retained and maintained for the life of the development.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;Prior to the first commencement of the use hereby permitted, all washing machines, dryers and associated mechanical plant and equipment , including any extraction systems, extract fans, tumble dryer, exhaust systems and associate motors, shall be installed with appropriate anti-vibration isolation measures and, where necessary, isolated from shared walls, floors, and ceilings in accordance with the submitted Noise and Vibration Impact Assessment. The approved measures shall thereafter be retained and maintained.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The cumulative rating level of noise emitted from all fixed mechanical plant and equipment associated with the use hereby permitted , including any ventilation, air conditioning, condenser units and extract systems, shall be at least 10 dB(A) below the representative background noise level at the nearest noise-sensitive premises, when assessed in accordance with BS4142:2024+A1:2019. The approved plant shall thereafter be retained and maintained.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ]
